;; RUNTIME-VALIDATION-CATALOG.edn -- worklist row :U36.
;;
;; Every runtime validation of the War Machine that can be PRODUCED TODAY with
;; evidence, organised per R node first (Joe 2026-09-03: per-node "is what was
;; really missing last time") and then per global run.
;;
;; WHAT A ROW IS. One validation: a named thing that can be RUN, that answers
;; about the machine's behaviour, and whose answer leaves an artifact. A row
;; names the validation, the pointer that locates it, the KIND of evidence it
;; produces, its STATUS as measured on 2026-09-03, and which J-gated flip it
;; becomes a gate line for (the U32 feed).
;;
;; WHAT A ROW IS NOT. It is not a claim that the validation is sufficient, and
;; it is not a ruling. Where a validation exists but its subject is planted
;; rather than recorded, the row says so in :provenance; where a validation is
;; missing, the row is :named-gap and carries the row id that owns the gap.
;;
;; STATUSES WERE MEASURED, NOT ASSERTED. Every :test-green row names a
;; namespace in :test-runs, and every entry of :test-runs is one recorded
;; invocation on 2026-09-03 with its exit code. 102 namespaces were run one
;; JVM each; the raw log is runs/U36-runtime-validation/test-run-2026-09-03.txt.
;; Three came back RED and are typed :red here rather than counted as coverage.
;;
;; POINTER CONVENTION. Every pointer is REPO-RELATIVE FROM /home/joe/code, with
;; an optional :LINE or :A-B. runtime_validation_check.bb resolves all of them
;; by direct path join. This is deliberately not pointer_check.bb's bare-filename
;; allowlist: this catalog cites five repositories and two test trees, which is
;; exactly the shape that made a valid pointer read as "file not found" six
;; times in that checker's own history (its header records C472, C473, AC7,
;; U11, U13, U23).
{:schema :wm/runtime-validation-catalog-v1
 :row :U36
 :as-of "2026-09-03"
 :owner :wm-organization
 :organizing-axis :per-node
 :heads {:futon2 "42a957c" :futon3c "17fde898"}
 :validator "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/runtime_validation_check.bb"
 :raw-run-log "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/U36-runtime-validation/test-run-2026-09-03.txt"

 :node-set [:R1 :R2 :R3 :R4 :R5 :R6 :R7 :R8 :R9 :R10 :R11 :R12 :R13 :R14 :R15
            :R16 :R17 :R20 :TRACE]
 :node-set-source
 "p4ng/empirics-futon/control-stages.edn:6-27 -- the drawn authority, 19 nodes
  including TRACE. R19 (the C/preference stack) is named in the Lean run
  witness (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:6592) and carries its own
  validations, but it is not a node of the drawn map, so its rows are
  :global-run rather than :per-node. Recorded as an observation about the two
  node vocabularies; no ruling."

 :vocabulary
 {:axis [:per-node :global-run]
  :evidence-kind [:test-green          ;; a test namespace that runs and passes
                  :replay-artifact     ;; a script re-run over recorded records, emitting a file
                  :typed-record        ;; a persisted record with a declared schema
                  :negative-control    ;; a planted defect the check must refuse
                  :not-yet-produced]   ;; the validation does not exist
  :status [:exists              ;; runs today and answers
           :exists-but-stale    ;; runs, but its subject or its pin has moved past it
           :red                 ;; runs and FAILS today
           :named-gap]          ;; nothing to run
  :substrate [:wm :zaif :fixture-only :cross :none]
  :binding [:self-declared        ;; the test's own docstring names the node
            :by-source-namespace  ;; the registry's :code names the ns this test covers
            :by-registry-row      ;; a row of aif-equations.edn or witness-registry.edn
            :by-run-record        ;; a recorded run/tick record
            :by-matrix]}          ;; U10's per-node matrix

